        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0796" n="686" xml:id="pg686"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Miller to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I hand you the report of the
                    district attorney for the eastern district of Louisiana, touching the
                    citizenship, etc., of the persons killed by the mob in New Orleans last month.
                    These I send direct to you, because it is a matter within the cognizance of your
                    Department, not mine.</p>
                <p>I have become satisfied that there is no statute of the United States under which
                    the persons responsible for this mob can be prosecuted in the Federal
                    courts.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. H. H. Milter</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Attorney-General</hi>.</signed></closer>











